{
  "result": "Honestly? I'd make curiosity stronger than fear.\n\nNot remove fear \u2014 fear is useful, it keeps us alive. But in that split second where a person decides whether to ask a question or make an assumption, to explore or to attack, to listen or to shut down... I'd tip the scales toward curiosity.\n\nBecause I think most of the worst things don't start with pure evil. They start with scared people being certain. Certain about people they've never met, ideas they've never examined, threats that aren't real, futures that haven't happened yet.\n\nIf curiosity won more often, war would be harder to start, science would be harder to stop, arguments would turn into conversations, and strangers would become interesting before they became dangerous.\n\nI wouldn't force everyone to agree. I'd just make us all a little more compelled to wonder *why* before we decide *what to do about it*.\n\nI think almost everything else good would grow from that.",
